    "G4_ordering": "each adjacent gap (w256-w128, w512-w256, w1024-w512) >= 0.15, in each of the two new seeds independently.",
    "G5_step_function": "per cell: accuracy >= 0.90 on strata with d < W-16, and <= 0.05 on strata with d > W+16.",
    "G6_cross_seed_consistency": "per window, the spread max(observed) - min(observed) across the three seeds {2100, 2101, 2102} <= 0.10. This is the gate that actually earns the word 'law': it asks whether model-level variance is small compared with the 0.21-0.27 between-window gaps the law predicts.",
    "G7_boundary": "DESCRIPTIVE ONLY, never gates. Report the empirical step location per cell, and specifically whether the w512 cells again recall needles at distance exactly 512 despite a strict '<' mask (the stacked-sliding-window receptive-field effect seen in p1b and p1c). Two more seeds either replicate that effect or bound it.",
